  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 mandates reporting of serious incidents within 24 hours and other confirmed overheating incidents within 5 business days, with customer notice within 5 business days. S2 sets a permanent 8% failure limit at 55 °C (above the 5% safe/acceptable level) but requires numerical per-model results to customers and regulators. S3 delays new-unit shut-off by 12 months and retrofit by 72 months with a regulator-approved alternative; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 sets a mandatory recall trigger at 10 per 100,000 (above the 8 safe/acceptable level) with regulator authority to act sooner."
 },
